'''"Bleeding Love"''' is a song [[Sound recording and reproduction|recorded]] by British singer [[Leona Lewis]] for her debut [[Album#Types of album|studio album]], ''[[Spirit (Leona Lewis album)|Spirit]]'' (2007).<ref name="popjustice">{{cite news|title=Leona Lewis: Basically a press release presented as "news"|url=http://www.popjustice.com/index.php?option=com_content&task=view&id=1492&Itemid=9|publisher=Popjustice|date=16 August 2007|access-date=16 August 2007}}</ref> It was originally written and recorded by American singer [[Jesse McCartney]], and was co-written and produced by American singer [[Ryan Tedder]].<ref name="notes">{{cite AV media notes|title= Bleeding Love|others = Leona Lewis|year = 2007 |type = CD Single|publisher  = Sony BMG|id= 88697175622}}</ref>{{efn|McCartney's version was later included as a bonus track on the international editions of his third studio album ''[[Departure (Jesse McCartney album)|Departure]]'' (2008).}} "Bleeding Love" was released worldwide during the last quarter of 2007, and the first of 2008, as the album's [[lead single]] internationally, and as the second single in Ireland and the United Kingdom.<ref name="hear">{{cite news|title=Hear Bleeding Love!|url=http://www.leonalewismusic.co.uk/Pages/NewsList.aspx?pageName=news&NewsID=39|date=14 September 2007|access-date=14 September 2007|archive-url=https://archive.today/20071211172429/http://www.leonalewismusic.co.uk/Pages/NewsList.aspx?pageName=news&NewsID=39|archive-date=11 December 2007|url-status=dead}}</ref> McCartney later included his version of the song as a [[Album#Tracks#Bonus tracks|bonus track]] on the international edition of his third studio album, ''[[Departure (Jesse McCartney album)|Departure]]'' (2008). It is Lewis' biggest hit, to date, and remains her [[List of signature songs|signature song]]. As of 2021, "Bleeding Love" has been [[Streaming media|streamed]] over two billion times.<ref>{{Cite web|last=TotalNtertainment|date=2 November 2021|title=Leona Lewis announces 'Christmas, With Love Always'|url=https://www.totalntertainment.com/music/leona-lewis-announces-christmas-with-love-always/|access-date=2021-11-18|website=TotalNtertainment}}</ref>

Debuting at number one on the [[Irish Singles Chart]] and [[UK Singles Chart]], "Bleeding Love" became the best-selling single of 2007 in both countries.<ref name="winehouseandlewis">{{cite news|url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/2/hi/entertainment/7165210.stm|title= Winehouse and Lewis head charts|publisher=BBC|access-date=30 December 2007 | date=31 December 2007}}</ref> After its release, the single became a massive success and was the world's best-selling single of 2008.<ref>[http://abc.go.com/music-lounge/artist/leona-lewis/346117 Leona Lewis – Music Lounge] {{Webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20111212133333/http://abc.go.com/music-lounge/artist/leona-lewis/346117 |date=12 December 2011 }} ABC. Retrieved 25 December 2011</ref> "Bleeding Love" reached number one in over 35 countries,<ref>[https://web.archive.org/web/20081116193755/http://www.ifpi.org/content/section_news/plat_month_20081022.html Platinum Awards] IFPI. October 2008.</ref> including France, Germany, Japan and the United States, making it only the second single in history to achieve this feat, [[Elton John]]'s "[[Candle in the Wind 1997|Candle in the Wind '97]]" being the first. The original accompanying music video first aired on 17 October 2007, and was uploaded to YouTube that same day. A second music video was premiered on 29 January 2008, on [[Yahoo! Music]] and was uploaded to YouTube the next day.

"Bleeding Love" has [[List of million-selling singles in the United Kingdom|sold more than one&nbsp;million copies in the United Kingdom]] and over 4 million digital downloads in the United States, where it was the best-selling digital song there in 2008.<ref name="bl4million">{{cite news|title = Week Ending June 6, 2010: "Surf's Up" And "Wipe Out" – Chart Watch| url = http://new.music.yahoo.com/blogs/chart_watch/55025/week-ending-june-6-2010-surfs-up-and-wipe-out/| publisher = [[Yahoo]]|date= 9 June 2010| access-date = 9 June 2010}}</ref><ref>{{cite magazine |author=Jonathan Cohen |url=http://www.billboard.biz/bbbiz/content_display/industry/news/e3i907e8f5ea24c29678d3f282a0af78468 |title=Lil Wayne Notches Top-Selling Album Of '08 |magazine=Billboard |date=31 December 2008 |access-date=24 February 2011 |archive-date=28 September 2011 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20110928055254/http://www.billboard.biz/bbbiz/content_display/industry/news/e3i907e8f5ea24c29678d3f282a0af78468 |url-status=dead }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=http://perezhilton.com/2009-07-27-lady-gaga-tops-the-tops-with-her-pop |title=Lady Gaga Tops The Tops With Her Pop |publisher=PerezHilton.com |date=27 July 2009 |access-date=31 August 2010 |archive-date=3 October 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181003061750/http://perezhilton.com/2009-07-27-lady-gaga-tops-the-tops-with-her-pop |url-status=dead }}</ref> It was named the 17th most successful song of the 2000s in the United States.<ref>{{cite magazine |url=http://www.billboard.com/bbcom/charts/chart_display.jsp?g=Singles&f=Greece#/charts-decade-end/hot-100-songs?year=2009&begin=11&order=position |title=Hot 100 Decade Songs |magazine=Billboard.com |access-date=24 February 2011 |archive-date=10 June 2008 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20080610074032/http://www.billboard.com/bbcom/charts/chart_display.jsp?g=Singles&f=Greece#/charts-decade-end/hot-100-songs?year=2009&begin=11&order=position |url-status=dead }}</ref> "Bleeding Love" has charted on the UK Singles Chart in three different years: at number one in 2007; number 76 in 2008; and at number 97 in 2009.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.officialcharts.com/search/singles/Trippin%20On%20You |title=Leona Lewis – Bleeding Love |publisher=[[Official Charts Company]] |access-date=31 August 2010}}</ref> It sold 788,000 copies in the United Kingdom alone during 2007.<ref>{{cite news| url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/2/hi/entertainment/7165210.stm | work=BBC News | title=Winehouse and Lewis head charts | date=31 December 2007 | access-date=26 April 2010}}</ref> "Bleeding Love" was nominated for [[Grammy Award for Record of the Year|Record of the Year]] and [[Grammy Award for Best Female Pop Vocal Performance|Best Female Pop Vocal Performance]] at the [[51st Annual Grammy Awards]]. It also received a nomination for Best British Single at the [[Brit Awards 2008|2008 Brit Awards]].<ref>[http://www.brits.co.uk/history/shows/2008 "The BRITs 2008"] {{Webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20121021165101/http://www.brits.co.uk/history/shows/2008 |date=21 October 2012 }} Brits.co.uk. Retrieved 6 November 2012</ref>

